-- title:
--   ̄ j(q^ℓ) lies in K(̄ j(q)) in characteristic ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $\ell$ be a prime number such that $K$ has characteristic $\ell$. Work inside the Laurent series field `LaurentSeries K` over $K$ (Hahn series over $K$ with value group $\mathbb{Z}$). Write $\bar j(q)$ for `jqModC K`, the element $q^{-1}$ — the Hahn series with single coefficient $1$ in degree $-1$ — multiplied by the power series `jNum` $= E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-style integral numerator (`eisenstein4 ^ 3 * dedekindEtaUnitInv` in $\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$) with its coefficients pushed into $K$ along the canonical map $\mathbb{Z} \to K$. Write $\bar j(q^{\ell})$ for `jqNModC K ℓ`, the image of $\bar j(q)$ under the ring homomorphism `qExpand K ℓ`, which reindexes a Laurent series along multiplication by $\ell$ on $\mathbb{Z}$, i.e. performs the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$. The assertion is that $\bar j(q^{\ell})$ belongs to the intermediate field `IntermediateField.adjoin K {jqModC K}` of $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by $\bar j(q)$.
--
--   This is the level-equals-characteristic case of the collapse of the function field generated by $q$-expansions of $j$ at level $N$: no modular-polynomial input is needed, because in characteristic $\ell$ substituting $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ in a series with prime-field coefficients is the same as raising to the $\ell$-th power. It is used in the proof that a $q$-expansion difference map on the modular function field is injective when the relevant theta-type invariant is non-zero.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_jqNModC_self_mem_adjoin_unconditional.lean

